        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Piano cover of embroidered silk damask, designed by C. R. Ashbee, England, ca. 1887."@en , "Piano cover of embroidered red silk damask with appliqué embroidery of a sunflower in green silk damask, and gold and white satin edged with connected gold thread and embroidered in coloured silk decorated with spangles. The petals are woven with a band of lettering inscribed with 'Joy and Gladness shall be Abound Therein - Thanks Giving and the Voice of Melody'."@en ;
